NOTE: the outer corrector used all 4 of its solves without converging on 8 of 624 time step(s) (reference = max(the step's predicted-state residual, corrector.atol/corrector.rtol)). Momentum/pressure missed control.yaml corrector.rtol=0.001 / corrector.atol=1e-10 on 8 step(s); the worst step ended at residual/reference=1.040e-03. Every step still ended below its reference residual, so this is NOT divergence: each step advanced, it just stopped short of the nonlinear tolerance. Stopping short means the nonlinear system was not solved to its tolerance, so the time-accuracy of the run is bounded by that ratio rather than by the tolerance; raise control.yaml corrector.max (or tighten the linear-solver tolerances feeding it) if you need the stated tolerance. See health.corrector_nonconverged, health.corrector_worst_res_ratio and the energy_corrector_* pair in the JSON summary.
